  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image juxtaposes a black-and-white photo of a smiling man and woman holding a tiger cub with the text 'we are all apart of god's plan. christ will come to us.' The visual of a tiger cub, an animal often associated with wildness and danger, is used in a religious context to create a jarring, ironic, or absurd contrast with the message of divine plan and Christ's return. This juxtaposition is likely intended to mock or satirize religious claims, particularly those related to prophecy or divine intervention, by presenting them alongside something that appears chaotic or out of place. The meme's intent is to provoke thought or laughter through absurdity, but it can be perceived as harmful because it trivializes or mocks religious beliefs, potentially offending believers. The overall intent is not abusive or cyberbullying toward a specific group, but it does carry a tone of irreverent mockery that may be considered disrespectful or blasphemous to some viewers, thus falling under the 'Harmful' category due to its potential to cause offense or undermine religious sentiment.",
